Android Studio can't run a main() from an Android module's test folder with the green arrow.
It builds a run script that looks for a source set named unitTest,
and Android projects don't have one. The JUnit test is unaffected and still runs normally.

The workaround is to compile and run the launcher from the terminal,
since the classes only use plain Java.
open the Terminal tab at the bottom, then run these commands from the project root (Windows):

cd app\src\test\java
javac -d ..\..\..\..\lf-out com\example\quarter2\minipeta3\ConsoleLauncher.java
java -cp ..\..\..\..\lf-out com.example.quarter2.minipeta3.ConsoleLauncher

in case of "javac" and "java" not being recognized by the terminal use

$env:Path += ";C:\Program Files\Android\Android Studio\jbr\bin"

then run
javac -d ..\..\..\..\lf-out com\example\quarter2\minipeta3\ConsoleLauncher.java
java -cp ..\..\..\..\lf-out com.example.quarter2.minipeta3.ConsoleLauncher
again